    "result_text": "The full suite consists of the two acceptance test files (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and both tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner resource, following the codebase's established pattern (OpenAPI-generated DTO + MapStruct `@Mapping` expression + a `protected` derivation method in `OwnerMapper`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema with an enum of the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), matching the documentation style of the neighbouring `contactPreference`/`ageBand` fields. This generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ...)` entry and an `ownerSegment(Owner)` method:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (reusing the existing `membershipLevel` derivation).\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when `locality(owner)` is one of `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, else `REGIONAL` (reusing the existing `locality` derivation).\n\nBoth are combined as `<TIER>_<AREA>` and resolved via the generated enum's `fromValue`.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) both pass, and the full build is green.",
